        "remediation": "<p>How to require session policies for Dropbox users</p> <ol> <li><a href=\"https://www.dropbox.com/login\">Sign in to dropbox.com</a>&nbsp;with your admin credentials.</li> <li>Click&nbsp;<strong>Admin Console</strong>.</li> <li>Click&nbsp;<strong>Settings</strong>.</li> <li>Under&nbsp;<strong>Additional Settings</strong>,<strong>&nbsp;</strong>click <strong>Web session control</strong>.</li> <li>Set the setting next to <strong>Fixed session length</strong> to <strong>1 week or less</strong>.</li> <li>It is also suggested, but not mandatory for compliance, to set the setting next to <strong>Idle session length</strong> to <strong>30 minutes&nbsp;or less</strong>.</li> <li>Click&nbsp;<strong>Save changes</strong>.</li> </ol>",
        "remediationImpact": "Once configured, some users may be automatically logged out and will be asked to log back in to Dropbox.",
